---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Span AI Solutions | Founders Josh Muller & Kamila Buitrago"
  description="Meet the founders of Span AI Solutions, a Regina, Saskatchewan team bridging the gap between people and their goals using AI."
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="hero section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <h1 id="about-title" class="hero-title">Bridging the gap between you and your goals.</h1>
        <p class="lead">We're Josh and Kamila, the founders of Span AI Solutions, based in Regina, Saskatchewan.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="founders-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <h2 id="founders-title" class="section-heading">Our founders</h2>
        <p class="section-copy">Josh builds the systems. Kamila makes sure they serve the people who use them. Together, we bring both the technical side and the human side of AI to every project.</p>
        <div class="cards cards--two">
          <article class="card">
            <img class="portrait-photo" src="/images/josh-muller.webp" width="640" height="480" alt="Josh Muller" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <h3>Josh Muller</h3>
            <p>Co-founder, AI Solutions, Product &amp; Strategy</p>
            <p>Josh has spent 18 years in technology, building systems that help small teams do big things. As Localization Director at Waha, he helps coordinate work across 180+ countries and 60+ languages. He has consulted for several of the world's top five expert networks and has been interviewed by El Espectador as an AI and technology expert. Today he helps businesses and individuals put AI to work in practical, reliable ways.</p>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thejoshmuller/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Josh Muller on LinkedIn (opens in a new tab)">Josh on LinkedIn →</a>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <img class="portrait-photo" src="/images/kamila-buitrago.webp" width="640" height="480" alt="Kamila Buitrago" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
            <h3>Kamila Buitrago</h3>
            <p>Co-founder, Sales &amp; Operations</p>
            <p>Kamila is a Colombian political scientist who has spent years coordinating humanitarian and social projects in Colombia and along the Türkiye–Syria border, earning the trust of communities, donors, NGOs, governments and international media. At Span, she leads client relationships, partnerships, operations and sales, making sure every project is clear, well-run and focused on what you actually need.</p>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kamilabuitrago/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Kamila Buitrago on LinkedIn (opens in a new tab)">Kamila on LinkedIn →</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="story-title">
      <div class="page-shell">
        <h2 id="story-title" class="section-heading">Why we started Span</h2>
        <div class="cards cards--two">
          <div>
        <p class="section-copy">For nine years, we worked side by side coordinating humanitarian and social projects in Türkiye, along the Türkiye–Syria border, and in Colombia. Again and again, we saw how much good a small team could do with the right tools and the right relationships, and how much was lost without them.</p>
        <p class="section-copy">We've built our lives around serving people. As AI became more capable and more accessible, we saw it as a new way to keep doing that. Used well, AI can serve people rather than replace them, and too many businesses and individuals are still on the other side of that gap. Span exists to bridge it.</p>
          </div>
          <img class="portrait-photo" src="/images/span-founders.webp" width="768" height="1152" alt="Span AI Solutions founders Josh Muller and Kamila Buitrago together" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="about-cta-title">
      <div class="page-shell cta-panel">
        <h2 id="about-cta-title" class="section-heading">Let's work together.</h2>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="/contact">Contact Us</a></div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
